DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TimelinePage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success over an injectable TimelineDataSource
seam (default = an API-response-shaped sample), driving four headline metric cards (Total Transitions / Driving /
Charging / Idle-Sleep time), a proportional State Distribution bar with an 8-state legend, a stacked Daily
Breakdown BarChart on the P3 Swift Charts wrapper (never a WKWebView), and a State Transitions DataTable with
computed per-state durations — adaptive across macOS/iPad sidebar width and iPhone compact width (ADR-002/006)
using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with web key names; full VoiceOver labels/traits on panels, bar, and rows; durations format
at the render boundary as SI seconds -> "Xh Ym". Deep-linkable via the new .timeline route (AppRouteParser resolves
/timeline automatically) and hosted through the shell's route registry. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6
strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness (72/72). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY
